# UBSan suppressions for the CI sanitizer job.
#
# One entry per KNOWN, UNFIXED finding, so that the job reports new diagnostics
# instead of re-reporting this one on every run. Deleting an entry is how the
# corresponding fix gets its regression check: once the defect is gone the
# suppression is unnecessary, and while the defect is present removing the line
# turns the job red again.
#
# Do not add anything here to make a build quiet. Each entry needs the finding
# written down next to it.

# src/logging.c:write_logs() reads the four-byte length prefix out of the ring
# buffer with
#
#     linelen = *(uint32_t *)&logger->log_buf[logger->read_idx];
#
# read_idx advances by whole messages, whose lengths are arbitrary, so the
# address is almost never 4-byte aligned. On x86-64 the load works and this is
# invisible; it is undefined behaviour regardless, and on a strict-alignment
# target it is a fault rather than a slow load. The wrapped branch immediately
# below it already does the right thing -- it assembles the length a byte at a
# time through a union -- so the fix is to take that path unconditionally, or
# to memcpy into a local.
#
# Reported by UBSAN as:
#   src/logging.c:128:21: runtime error: load of misaligned address ...
#     for type 'uint32_t', which requires 4 byte alignment
alignment:src/logging.c
